&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based at our London HQ, following a 3-day hybrid schedule. You will bring together two engineering organisations into one unified team, run our largest engineering hub outside of Sydney, and serve as the primary engineering partner for our UK commercial and product leaders. Reporting to the CTO in Sydney, you will work closely with executives in London and operate with the clarity and self-direction that distance requires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unify two orgs into one.&lt;/strong&gt; The team is 35 engineers across two engineering organisations, growing towards 50. You will manage six to eight direct reports (all engineering managers) and establish a unified standard for how both teams plan, build, ship, and hold each other accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the London engineering site.&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the senior engineering voice in the building, including dotted-line support for US-focused teams based in London. That means setting the tone, facilitating local leadership forums, and making London a place where exceptional engineers join and stay.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate commercial outcomes.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner directly with UK commercial, clinical, and product leaders as a true peer. You will serve as the primary contact across the business, evaluating trade-offs through a commercial lens and communicating them rather than escalating them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape what we build, not just how.&lt;/strong&gt; Evaluate whether proposed initiatives deliver real value and instil that thoughtful product instinct across your management team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and mentor the team.&lt;/strong&gt; Own senior hiring in London, set clear quality standards, and mentor engineering managers to become skilled hiring partners who can recruit effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise engineering standards.&lt;/strong&gt; Strengthen delivery predictability, quality, and operational reliability across a distributed organisation spanning Sydney, London, and the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve managed an engineering organisation of 30+ people through managers, with at least five years of experience developing other managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience guiding an organisation through significant structural change such as an integration, restructure, or operational overhaul where teams emerged stronger. You can reflect openly on the parts that went badly and what you learned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI tooling in your own work, and you&#39;ve changed how a team builds with it rather than just your own workflow. You can say what it made better, what it made worse, and where you chose not to use it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve demonstrated commercial fluency, holding constructive conversations on revenue, margin, and prioritisation while making speed, scope, and risk trade-offs clear and explicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building and scaling systems from the ground up, rather than simply maintaining a machine that already runs itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are technically strong and partner credibly with senior engineers, you evaluate system architecture, and spot when technical estimates lack substance. Coding is not the job, but you are comfortable getting on the tools to prototype an idea or unblock your team, and you can govern an ecosystem built on React, React Native, TypeScript, Go microservices, GraphQL, Kubernetes, and GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable managing a site distant from headquarters across various time zones. You leverage asynchronous communication, operating with high agency, independence, and clarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated sectors (such as healthtech, fintech or gaming), finding creative paths forward inside compliance constraints rather than being stopped by them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating post-acquisition organisational integration and the messy alignment work that follows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why join Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s next&lt;/strong&gt; - Our goal for the next three years is to support 1 million patients globally to live better for longer, launching into new conditions, demographics and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build something world-changing&lt;/strong&gt; - We&#39;re on the path to becoming the world&#39;s largest international digital healthcare company. It will be challenging, fast-paced and deeply rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make real impact&lt;/strong&gt; - Your work directly shapes patient outcomes and scales evidence-based care across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate your growth&lt;/strong&gt; - High ownership, continuous feedback and dedicated development support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a motivated team&lt;/strong&gt; - Talented peers solving complex clinical and operational problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What&#39;s ahead in the UK&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be an owner&lt;/strong&gt; - Your own stake in the business with our employee options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invest in your growth&lt;/strong&gt; - Annual development budget plus 3 days of professional development leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work flexibly&lt;/strong&gt; - Hybrid setup with 3 days a week in our Old Street office, designed for focus and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your well-being&lt;/strong&gt; - Private health insurance through Vitality, or a monthly wellness allowance to spend on what matters most to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take time off&lt;/strong&gt; - 25 days of holiday, enhanced parental leave and work from anywhere 3 weeks a year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a connected team&lt;/strong&gt; - A vibrant office culture with regular socials, clubs, after-school sport and seasonal events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Professional Services Technical Architect at GitLab, you&#39;ll lead the technical direction of customer engagements from early scoping and discovery through delivery. You&#39;ll design high-level architectures and implementation plans for GitLab infrastructure and functionality, and you&#39;ll make sure deliverables align with customer requirements and the Statement of Work (SOW). You&#39;ll coordinate and guide implementation work across GitLab Professional Services and partner consultants, support customers deploying GitLab in cloud and on-premises environments using tools like Terraform, Ansible, and the GitLab Environment Toolkit, and perform migrations to GitLab using Congregate. You&#39;ll provide DevOps and DevSecOps consulting and best practices, contribute reusable collateral such as documentation, delivery kits, and training materials, and share product release updates to help the team deliver consistent outcomes. This role combines deep technical expertise with customer-facing leadership in GitLab&#39;s remote, asynchronous, and values-driven environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and delivering GitLab reference architecture implementations for both self-managed and cloud environments, using infrastructure as code practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading source code management and CI/CD migrations to GitLab, including large-scale enterprise moves using Congregate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building repeatable delivery kits, documentation, and enablement materials that help Professional Services and partners deploy and adopt GitLab best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full technical delivery lifecycle for GitLab Professional Services engagements, from early scoping and technical discovery through implementation and handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce high-level and detailed technical designs for GitLab infrastructure and functionality, ensuring deliverables align with customer requirements and expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and communicate scalability and security considerations (including compliance constraints) in proposed GitLab reference architectures and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy and configure GitLab in customer environments, including on-premises and major cloud providers, using Terraform, Ansible, and the GitLab Environment Toolkit (GET) aligned to reference architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute source system migrations to GitLab using Congregate, partnering closely with customer stakeholders to reduce risk, protect data integrity, and minimize downtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide DevOps and DevSecOps consulting and best-practice guidance, including advising on internal frameworks such as the Delivery Governance Framework (DGF) and GitLab Flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and oversee implementation work across GitLab team members, partners, and customer points of contact (POCs), ensuring clear asynchronous communication and decision capture, effective execution, and high-quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor Professional Services and partner consultants by contributing documentation, delivery kits, and training materials, and by leading enablement sessions on how to deliver and position service offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve delivery automation assets with an emphasis on code cleanliness, maintainability, and appropriate unit/integration testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support scoping and Statement of Work (SOW) creation with Professional Services Engagement Managers, stay current on monthly GitLab releases, and help Regional Delivery Managers with technical vetting and staffing assessments while maintaining a 55% billable utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and provide input to Professional Services training materials and presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop case studies, presentations, design documentation, and best-practice methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with customer project teams to ensure accurate task-level articulation of work required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to lead technical discussions with customers and partners and communicate risks/trade-offs clearly in an asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UK remote based role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 50% travel at times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience delivering two or more of the following consulting services: source code management migration, cloud architecture, DevOps engineering, or continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) consulting services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise software development experience, with the ability to translate requirements into clear technical designs and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive DevOps platform experience, including designing and implementing reliable, scalable systems with clear performance and security trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience deploying and managing infrastructure in cloud providers and on-premises environments, including using tools such as Terraform and Ansible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write clean, maintainable automation/integration code (e.g., Terraform modules, Ansible roles, scripts) and validate changes with appropriate testing and code review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing migrations to GitLab, including using Congregate or similar migration tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data consistency and integrity concepts (e.g., ACID properties) and how they impact migration design and performance trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, decision-making, organizational, and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in a remote, asynchronous environment, using documented decisions (e.g., issues, proposals, and runbooks) to keep work unblocked across time zones while collaborating effectively across GitLab team members, partners, and customer stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or other advanced technical degree, or equivalent experience.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; #LI-CM1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Professional Services Technical Architect is part of GitLab&#39;s Professional Services organization. We partner with customers who are transitioning to GitLab, expanding how they use an existing GitLab installation, or planning complex upgrades to their infrastructure and processes. Our team brings a diverse set of skills across GitLab deployment, maintenance, and day-to-day usage, along with deep technical knowledge of adjacent tools and platforms. Working closely with Engagement Managers, partner consultants, and customer stakeholders, we focus on delivering high-quality outcomes, sharing best practices, and helping customers realize faster time to value from their GitLab investment. We operate in GitLab&#39;s remote, asynchronous environment and rely on clear documentation and transparent communication to collaborate effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role models skills and behaviour aligned with GitLab Values and typically reports to the Regional Delivery Manager. As a Professional Services Technical Architect, you will work more independently than an associate consultant, leveraging deep technical expertise to drive customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About THG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are THG, a global ecommerce group on a mission to be the global online leader in beauty and sports nutrition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our portfolio of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; leading retailers and brands such as LOOKFANTASTIC, Myprotein, ESPA, Perricone MD, and Cult Beauty form our two core businesses: THG Beauty and THG Nutrition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;From Manchester to New York, we’re powered by a team of over 2500 people who work together, lead by example, and think BIG.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;With us, you’ll go further, faster. What are you waiting for?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Icon 1, WA15 0AF&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at THG Beauty&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know that beauty isn’t one-size-fits-all. Our portfolio of leading retailers and iconic beauty brands caters to everyone, everywhere, empowering customers all over the world to look and feel fantastic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining our portfolio of owned brands inclusive of ESPA, Ameliorate and Christophe Robin, with a marketplace for over 1,300 third-party beauty brands through online retail sites LOOKFANTASTIC, Cult Beauty, and Dermstore, THG Beauty&#39;s ambition is to be the global digital partner of choice across the beauty industry, supporting the channel shift to online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;THG Beauty’s breadth of relationships is unique to the beauty market; it engages with brands as a retailer, a brand owner, and a product developer and manufacturer, making it the industry’s digital strategic leader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Why be a Senior Analyst — Customer (Beauty) at THG?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Analyst in the Beauty Customer team, you will own analytical work that helps THG’s Beauty division understand and grow its customer base. Working across acquisition, retention, CRM, marketing and loyalty, you will build the analysis, models and insight that enable the business to make better decisions about how it acquires and retains customers. You are expected to work largely independently — owning complex analytical problems end-to-end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Analyst — Customer (Beauty)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;, you will: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own analytical projects across the customer lifecycle — acquisition, retention, CRM, loyalty, marketing performance and personalisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build customer segmentations, cohort analyses and behavioural models that the business can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse marketing channel performance — understanding what drives efficient acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of the Beauty customer KPI framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to marketing mix modelling (MMM) — providing customer and channel inputs, and connecting MMM outputs back to customer-level acquisition and retention decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesise quantitative data with qualitative insight (customer research, surveys, feedback) to build a rounded view of customer behaviour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain SQL queries and analytical scripts — producing accurate, well-documented analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Engineering team to understand the customer data model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and reports that communicate customer performance clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present findings to the Customer Lead and Beauty stakeholders — translating complex analysis into clear business recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ad hoc analytical requests — prioritising effectively and delivering reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the Customer Analyst — sharing knowledge and providing feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships across Beauty, Marketing, Brand and Data Engineering — managing stakeholder expectations and competing priorities proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What skills and experience do I need for this role?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience (typically 3+ years) in customer analytics, CRM or marketing analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills — comfortable building complex analytical queries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with customer segmentation, cohort analysis or lifecycle analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong storytelling — able to communicate complex analysis clearly to non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently and take end-to-end ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ecommerce analytics — conversion, funnel and site performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at synthesising quantitative data with qualitative insight to form a complete view of customer behaviour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management — able to build trust and manage competing priorities across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in beauty, lifestyle, fashion or e-commerce environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to marketing mix modelling (MMM) or econometric approaches to marketing measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CRM or marketing automation platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Tableau or equivalent BI tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Good Looks Like at This Level&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At THG, we expect everyone to demonstrate behaviours that match their level. Here is what that looks like in this role:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operates largely independently — owns complex customer analytics end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in customer analytics — the go-to person for customer behaviour, acquisition and retention questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coaches the Customer Analyst — actively developing team capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for own targets — delivers high-quality analysis with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
